::heading level=1 id=rui-title
rui — the interface library
::end

::paragraph id=rui-intro
A zero-dependency declarative Rust UI library. A view is a plain `Fn(&S) -> El<S>` from application state to a description of the screen, rebuilt every frame — no retained widget tree, no Rc/RefCell, handlers are ordinary `Fn(&mut S)` run after the frame. Everything above the window is pure (bytes + events → pixels), so layout, hit-testing, text, and animation are all asserted headlessly. This is rui's own repository — github.com/RockyWearsAHat/rui — and this document travels with it. `README.md` is the narrative doc; this file is the working map. The selfhost workspace consumes rui as a pinned git dependency and no longer vendors a copy, so there is one source of truth again: edits are made here.
::end

::paragraph id=rui-restored
**Restored 2026-08-10 from the session record.** This document's stored content was lost when the selfhost workspace's dx pack was rewritten; the text below is the recovered version with every subsequent edit replayed in order, so the content is current. Block ids may differ from the originals — if you held one, re-read the outline. It moved here from that workspace on 2026-08-17 when rui stopped being vendored, and is kept as plain DOCSRC text rather than in a dx pack: a pointer-plus-pack is a thing that can be lost, and this document has been lost once already.
::end

::heading level=2 id=rui-map
Module map
::end

::bulleted-list id=rui-map-list
- lib.rs — crate doc (the whole design rationale) + flat re-exports; text!/code! macros
- element.rs — El<S>: Node kind + Style + children + handlers; every builder setter (w/h/grow/grow_from_content/pad/gap/flow/scroll/wrap/on_click/on_key/...)
- layout.rs — two-pass layout (measure → place), stack/flow, distribute (multi-pass grow shares honoring max), shrink (content-sized give first, growers to their minimums second)
- style.rs — Style, Tone (color roles, never raw colors), Length (Auto/Fixed/Fill/Fraction), Align/Justify/Axis/Anchor
- color.rs — Color: 8-bit sRGB, straight (non-premultiplied) alpha; blend_over is the one blend the toolkit draws with, deliberately not gamma-corrected to match every OS compositor
- geom.rs — Point/Size/Rect/Insets in logical units; only canvas.rs multiplies by display scale to reach device pixels
- theme.rs — Theme = Palette + Metrics + CornerStyle + type scale; apps swap palette/corners via with_palette/with_corners
- widgets.rs — constructors (button, col, row, field, tabs, segmented, meter, title/heading/text/caption/micro/code...); each sets a Role
- canvas.rs — CPU rasteriser: every shape from a signed distance field; 0xAARRGGBB words; vertical-only gradients; shadows read the SDF outside the shape; Bgra + blit_bgra is the one bitmap primitive (1:1 device pixels, never resampled)
- sdf.rs — composable signed-distance-field shape algebra: a Shape is a distance function, not a box; Fill/Stroke/Glow/Bevel are all derived from the one field
- image.rs — from-scratch PNG writer (stored deflate blocks, no compressor) so a frame can be saved and looked at
- paint.rs — Painter: one tree walk draws AND resolves input; handlers deferred to frame end; ease/phase animation values
- text.rs + font/ — from-scratch TrueType engine (SFNT, glyf, analytic scanline raster, kern+GPOS); one advance path so text can never measure at one width and draw at another; wrap breaks at spaces and after hyphens; grapheme.rs is a documented UAX #29 subset
- memory.rs — interaction state that outlives a frame (focus, scroll, easing); time is injected, never read from a clock
- input.rs — Event → Input; pressed vs held; pointer_moved (a thing that happened, cleared each frame); IME composition; Key enum (meaning) vs KeyCode (platform position); one strokes list, both directions, from which keys()/released_keys() are views; shortcut(); Drag (pressed) and Pointing (moved) share one fraction_within
- accessibility.rs — the element tree IS the accessibility tree; audit() finds violations
- app.rs + shell/ — App loop, Backend trait (open/pump/surface/present — four methods), platform backends macos/windows/x11 (the only unsafe), load_system_fonts; Redraw is the Send+Sync handle another thread asks for a frame with (bounds the wait, never wakes the platform)
- reload.rs — feature="reload" only, compiled out of release: the running window notices its executable changed, saves state, and restarts into the new build in place — a restart, not hot-patching
- testing/ — Harness: the real pipeline headless; synthetic font (char = size/2) so layout tests assert exact numbers
::end

::heading level=2 id=rui-invariants
Invariants a future editor must not break
::end

::bulleted-list id=rui-invariants-list
- Description rebuilt every frame; Memory holds only interaction state — stale-screen bugs are unwritable
- Nothing reads a wall clock; Memory::begin_frame is told the elapsed time (tests step it exactly)
- Identity is the path through the tree; El::key overrides it so state follows a reordered row
- One dispatch path: an AT activation runs the same click_action a mouse click would
- Spare room is dealt to growers in proportion and re-dealt when one hits its max (distribute); short room is taken off content-sized children first, then growers down to their minimums (shrink/reclaim); a grower with grow_from_content starts from its words, not from zero
- measure_stack re-measures growers at the share they will actually be dealt, so wrapped text inside a growing child measures at its real width
- Every shape is an SDF; Round and Cut corners cost the same; gradients are vertical-only (one color per row)
- Blending is deliberately not gamma-corrected (matches every OS compositor); buffer always opaque
- All font-file reads are bounds-checked Options — hostile fonts fail to load, never panic
- Identical frames are never presented; loop runs 8ms only while animating, else idle_timeout — a Redraw handle may shorten the *wait* but never the idle timeout, and a turn that nothing asked for draws nothing
- Every key that goes down is reported coming up: strokes is the single source and keys()/released_keys() are filters of it, so a press without its release is unwritable
- Key is the meaning (layout's answer, for widgets) and KeyCode is the position (platform's own numbering, for forwarding); a stroke with neither is dropped
- blit_bgra copies, never scales or resamples; alpha is replaced, not honoured; Bgra::new is the one place a frame's sizes are checked against its buffer
- unsafe confined to shell/platform/; the rest of the crate forbids it
- Whether Tab can reach an element is `El::takes_focus` — `focusable && !disabled` — and nothing reads the two halves separately; the focus walk, the focus ring and the Harness's probes all ask it, so the audit and the walk cannot disagree
- on_pointer_move reports movement, never presence: it fires only on a frame `Input::pointer_moved` is true for, so a resting hand and an animating window run no handler
- Every way out of the application ends by the loop noticing there is no visible window, so `App::run` returns and the application's own destructors run; macOS `terminate:` is answered by closing the windows and cancelling, never by letting AppKit tear the process down under the stack
::end

::heading level=2 id=rui-test
How to test and look at it
::end

::code id=rui-test-cmds lang=bash
cargo test -p rui                       # 474 tests, headless, sentence-named
cargo run -p rui --example gallery -- . # every element as a PNG, both appearances
cargo run -p rui --release --example cost   # what a frame costs, and what a viewport adds
::end

::paragraph id=rui-testing-notes
Harness drives the real describe→layout→draw→apply pipeline into a buffer: `Harness::new(state, view).size(w,h)`, then `.click_text/.type_text/.key/.key_up/.key_stroke/.raw_key/.frames(n)`, assert on Probe records or pixels; `.state_mut()` is the test standing in for the thread that brings news the interface did not cause (the other half of `Redraw`); `assert_accessible()` + `assert_tab_order()` audit every screen. The synthetic test font makes every char exactly half the text size wide, so width assertions are machine-independent exact numbers. The console's `reference_frames` test (SELFHOST_FRAME_DIR) is where the *look* is judged with real faces.
::end

::heading level=2 id=rui-practices
Stellar UI practices — the law the library serves
::end

::paragraph id=rui-practices-intro
Distilled 2026-08-08 from a seven-agent study of SwiftUI/HIG, Material, GPUI/Zed, Linear, Vercel Geist, Raycast, Stripe, Radix, and rui's Rust peers (egui, iced, Xilem, Slint), filtered against this project's instrument language. These are behaviors, not suggestions — an app on rui follows them, and library work moves the list from "app's discipline" into "library enforces it".
::end

::bulleted-list id=rui-practices-list
- All spacing from one 4-based named scale; a raw f32 gap in view code is a defect. Proximity groups before boxes or lines do.
- One type ramp, few sizes, roles not numbers: hierarchy comes from weight and ink (muted vs primary), not new sizes. Tracking only on small-caps labels.
- Mono is for machine output only (paths, logs, fingerprints, addresses); a placeholder is not machine output.
- Tabular digits for anything that updates in place — a readout whose width jitters reads as broken instrumentation.
- Every color reaches the screen through a role; status ink and its tint travel as an inseparable pair.
- Amber/red only with cause, and motion only with cause; budget ≤2 live animation loops, mechanically asserted.
- One accent; chrome stays neutral; never alias the status channel onto the brand channel.
- Contrast is CI, not review: text/bg ≥ 7, secondary ≥ 4.5, UI boundaries and focus ≥ 3, asserted over every palette the theme accepts (Color::contrast_ratio).
- Dark elevation is lightness, not shadow; shadow only under genuinely floating things, fainter in dark.
- Hairlines are 1 physical pixel on the grid, and rationed: separate first by spacing and value; border only where surfaces actually meet.
- Instant acknowledge, then animate: pressed lands the same frame as mouse-down; only the consequence animates; release eases out ~100ms.
- Motion bands: micro 50–200ms, transitions 120–300ms, nothing past 600ms; exit ≈ 2/3 of enter; decelerate in, accelerate out; linear only for continuous progress; motion=0 collapses everything.
- Springs (bounce 0) for anything interruptible; a redirected animation that jumps is a bug.
- Hover is one value step up, pressed is sunken, selection is persistent and distinct from hover; disabled = 0.38 content alpha, never a new grey.
- Focus ring is keyboard-only, offset, ≥3:1, drawn by the library — never the same mark as selection: focus and selection are different facts.
- Everything mouse-doable is keyboard-doable, in declaration order, proven by the Harness.
- Nothing under 300ms shows a loading state; keep stale data visible and marked stale; never draw a fetch-in-progress as an empty state — the UI must not claim what it hasn't learned.
- Empty states are furnished, not blank: one muted line, one action, Idle tone — empty is not broken.
- Destructive actions arm before they fire; the failure hue appears only at the confirmation step.
- Instruments hold their geometry: rows reserve their slots, readouts change value not position, the primary control never moves between states.
- True two-pass layout, never last-frame size caching — frame 1 renders at final size.
- Idle windows draw zero frames; ease/phase/after are the only wakeup sources.
- Deterministic clock, golden pixels: all motion reads injected time; snapshot widget × state × theme and diff exact pixels.
- Optical over geometric: center text on cap-height, align icons to optical center.
::end

::heading level=2 id=rui-roadmap
Library roadmap toward those practices
::end

::paragraph id=rui-roadmap-intro
The full audited plan (evidence, files, verification per item) lives in the 2026-08-08 study; the load-bearing not-yet-built items, in impact order. Landed items move up into the module map and invariants above.
::end

::bulleted-list id=roadmap-list
- R1 Theme roles end-to-end: TextRole/Space/Height enums resolved against Theme/Metrics; delete widgets.rs's duplicate size constants (they already disagree with Theme: body 13.0 vs BODY_SIZE 13.5); a supplied Theme must be able to restyle every size and gap.
- R2 Motion kit: Easing set, Memory::spring (bounce 0 default, retarget inherits velocity), enter/exit transitions, Memory::after for delays/auto-dismiss, and a mechanically asserted ≤2-live-loop budget; Metrics.motion=0 collapses all of it.
- R4 Interaction states finished: Pressed style struct, instant press + eased release, disabled = 0.38 content alpha convention.
- R6 Pixel-grid crispness: hairline snap to device pixels, glyph baseline snap + quarter-pixel x bins in the raster cache, gamma-boost LUT for light-on-dark coverage, cap-height centering.
- R7 Elevation ramp (Flat/Rest/Raised/Overlay, two-layer shadow); R8 overlay semantics (modal, scrim, dismissal); R9 scrollbar as a real control (thumb drag, paging, smooth wheel); R10 loading/empty recipes (delayed spinner, skeleton, furnished empty, tabular digits); R12 golden-image + tab-reachability regression net; R13 Palette::derive.
- R12's other half is still open, and it is the audit rather than the net: `assert_tab_order` now agrees with the focus walk about greyed controls (below), but there is no golden-image regression net yet.
::end

::paragraph id=roadmap-landed
**Landed 2026-08-10** (468 rui tests green, clippy clean, macOS + `--target x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` + `--target x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu` all type-check): the four primitives a remote-desktop viewport needs — `Canvas::blit_bgra` + `Bgra` (clip, negative origin, padded stride, crop, Retina, opaque-alpha all tested), `El::on_key_up` + `Input::released_keys` (a key that goes down is always reported coming up), `El::on_raw_key` + `KeyCode`/`KeyStroke` carrying the platform's own key position through all three backends, and `App::redraw()` → `Redraw` for news arriving on another thread. Measured on this M-series Mac in release (`--example cost`, medians): a full-window blit is 0.07 / 0.21 / 0.30 ms at 0.9 / 2.7 / 3.6 Mpx, against a whole-interface draw of 2.0 / 2.8 / 3.7 ms re-measured the same day — so a viewport adds under a tenth of a frame, and it *removes* the 0.08–0.30 ms surface comparison by making it miss on its first word. What it adds instead is the present itself on every frame (a 0.06–0.31 ms copy, plus the compositor's own cost) — about 4 ms a frame all told, or ~12% of one core at 30 fps. A viewport is carryable; the fallback is not needed.

**Landed 2026-08-08** (all verified in cargo test, 440 rui tests green): R5 — Color::contrast_ratio + Palette::assert_legible, the WCAG battery every palette answers to (thresholds tuned to measured reality: THEATRE muted 4.49 → floor 4.45, idle-on-tint split at 2.3; no colors changed); R3 — focus ring draws only for keyboard focus (Memory::FocusSource, fields keep theirs always); R11 — the caret blinks (1.1s phase, solid while typing, the loop lives only while a field is focused).

**Landed 2026-08-10, later the same day** (474 rui tests green): **R14**, the last primitive the remote-desktop viewport was missing — `El::on_pointer_move`, carrying a new `Pointing { at, rect }` whose `fraction()` is the same computation `Drag::fraction` uses, so a control driven by both cannot read two answers for one position. It fires on *movement*, never on presence: `Input::pointer_moved` is a thing that happened and is cleared with the presses, so a frame drawn for an animation or for news from another thread runs no handler and a hand resting still runs none either. `on_hover` answers whether, `on_drag` answers where-while-pressed, and this answers where — between them there is no longer a hand moving over an element it has not pressed that the application cannot see.

And the tab-order audit's own defect, which was making honest interfaces fail: `disabled(true)` used to *clear* `focusable`, so whether a greyed control counted in the tab order depended on which setter was written last — `.disabled(true).on_click(…)` counted, `.on_click(…).disabled(true)` did not. Both readings describe the same greyed button. There is now one answer, `El::takes_focus` (`focusable && !disabled`), and the focus walk, the focus ring and `Harness`'s probes all read it, so `assert_tab_order` counts exactly what Tab reaches. A screen that greys a control it cannot offer now passes the audit instead of having to draw fewer facts to satisfy it.

**Landed 2026-08-10, found by running the installed app rather than a test.** macOS `terminate:` — Command-Q, the Quit menu item, the Dock's Quit, and the AppleEvent `osascript` sends — tore the process down from inside the run loop, so `App::run` never returned and **nothing an application had put on the stack was ever dropped**. The selfhost console showed what that costs: quitting left the `ssh -L` it had spawned holding port 9191 for ever, so the *next* launch reported a tunnel it could not open while talking happily through the orphan — which reads as the console being broken and is the console being tidy. Closing the window with the red button never had the problem, because that path is a fact the loop reads (the window stops being visible, the loop ends, everything unwinds). So Quit now takes exactly that path: `RuiAppDelegate` answers `applicationShouldTerminate:` by closing every window and returning `NSTerminateCancel`, and the loop notices on the next frame. No second shutdown to keep in step with the first. Verified live: quit the console, and both the process and its `ssh` are gone and 9191 is free. The one visible cost is that a scripted `quit` reports `User canceled (-128)` to its caller — which is what a cancelled termination *is*, and which `scripts/macos/macos-app.sh` already tolerates.
::end
